0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.5.0 and 4.4.1.\n\n### System information\n\nTested on both Windows 10 and Zorin Linux distro\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe engine crashes with no debug information when a child class's override method signature does not match the parent method's signature, and the returned value is null.\n\nFrom my perspective, there are two obvious possible fixes. I'd be fine with either.\n1. This should be a compiler error, or at least a warning. The child class's method should be marked as needing to have the same return type as (or ideally, any subtype of) the parent class's.\n2. When a crash like this happens, an exception should be thrown that indicates the chain of calls which failed and why, instead of a silent crash.\n\nThank you for your time.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nParentClass.gd:\n```\nclass_name ParentClass\n\nfunc get_array() -> Array:\n\treturn []\n```\n\nChildClass.gd:\n```\nextends ParentClass\n\nclass_name ChildClass\n\nfunc get_array():\n\treturn null\n```\n\nCode that crashes:\n```\nvar my_array_getter: ParentClass = ChildClass.new()\n\nfunc on_button_press():\n\tvar thing := my_array_getter.get_array()\n\tif thing == null:\n\t\tprint(\"Thing is null\")\n\t\treturn\n\t\n\tprint(str(thing.size()) + \" // \" + str(thing))\n```\n\nFrom my debugging, please note the following happens:\n1. `thing` gets set to null, despite being of type 'Array`.\n2. The if-check fails, and decides that `thing != null`, even though in the debugger, the value of `thing` is `<null>`.\n3. The crash happens on the `print` line.\n\nI had previously thought I was safe because the `if` should have caught this, but in practice it fails.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[empty-array-crash-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22867633/empty-array-crash-test.zip)","closed_by":